# CampusFix IT Platform — Evolution & Implementation Plan

## Executive Summary

This plan outlines the end-to-end evolution of the existing **CampusFix AI** project into the comprehensive **CampusFix IT Platform (University Helpdesk & Incident Resolver)**.

The evolution maintains **100% backward compatibility** with the current FastAPI backend, OpenRouter integration, NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra AI reasoning engine, `/api/chat` workflow, and ticket state persistence while expanding into an enterprise-grade university IT service management system.

---

## Architectural Principles & Integrity Guarantees

1. **Preserve Existing Core**:
   - Backend `/api/chat`, `/api/health`, `/api/tickets`, and `/api/status` endpoints remain active and fully functional.
   - `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` remains strictly protected on the backend server (`backend/.env`). No secrets or keys will ever be exposed to the client.
   - NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra stays configured as the primary AI diagnostic reasoning engine.
2. **Dynamic Reactive State**:
   - Creating, resolving, or escalating tickets immediately updates the global state, Kanban board, Incident History, Admin Overview metrics, and Host Reports.
   - Demo/sample data is clearly labeled and seamlessly merges with live user-generated tickets.
3. **Enterprise UI/UX Design System**:
   - Dark mode & Light mode theme switching powered by CSS variables and local storage persistence.
   - Polished 18–24px rounded cards, glassmorphism overlays, subtle glow effects, smooth transitions, micro-animations, and responsive layouts across desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - All existing backend routes (`/api/chat`, `/api/health`, `/api/tickets`, `/api/status`) will remain intact with zero breaking changes.
> - The Host role will be strictly **read-only**, isolated exclusively to Reports with all administrative and mutation actions disabled.
> - The AI diagnostic specialist will remain fully powered by **NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra** via OpenRouter.

